operation, responsibility.\n\nLet's assess each candidate based on our notes:\n\nA:\n- Reliability: anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, leadership qualities. But unfriendly, eats unhealthily (maybe health concerns). No explicit reliability statement.\n- Technical competence: spatial vision, complex connections, anticipation. Good.\n- Calmness under pressure: not mentioned.\n- Cooperation: unfriendly (negative).\n- Responsibility: leadership qualities, but no explicit responsibility.\n\nB:\n- Reliability: very conscientious (good), handles stress well (calmness), good at assessing weather (technical), excellent computer skills (technical). Pretentious, wrong tone (cooperation issues). No explicit reliability but conscientious suggests reliability.\n- Calmness: handles stress well.\n- Cooperation: pretentious, wrong tone.\n- Responsibility: not explicit.\n\nC:\n- Reliability: can make correct decisions quickly (decision quality), puts concern for others above everything (cooperation), excellent attention skills (attention). Difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education (development). So reliability good, cooperation maybe mixed due to egocentric but also concern for others.\n- Calmness: not explicit but quick correct decisions may imply calmness.\n- Technical competence: not explicit but attention skills.\n- Responsibility: not explicit.\n\nD:\n- Reliability: responds to unexpected events adequately (reliability), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), solves problems extremely well (technical competence), concentration (attention). Moody, loner (cooperation). No explicit stress resilience but \"responds to unexpected events adequately\" suggests some resilience.\n- Cooperation: moody, loner (negative).\n\nNow we need to decide which candidate best fits overall. All have some concerns. Which candidate has the strongest overall fit? Let's weigh.\n\nCandidate B: strong stress handling, conscientious, technical (weather, computer). But communication issues (pretentious, wrong tone). Could be mitigated? But crew cooperation is crucial. Also no explicit reliability beyond conscientiousness.\n\nCandidate D: strong technical competence, responsibility, concentration, problem solving. But moody, loner, possibly weak leadership. Could affect crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate C: quick correct decisions, attention skills, concern for others, positive crew atmosphere (not in our notes but we have \"puts concern for others above everything\" which suggests cooperation). Communication difficulty and egocentric may hinder crew cooperation. Not willing to further education may affect adaptability.\n\nCandidate A: strong anticipation, complex connections, leadership, but unfriendly, unhealthy. No stress handling evidence.\n\nGiven the criteria, I think Candidate C might be the best overall: decision quality, attention, concern for others, reliability (quick correct decisions). Communication difficulty is a concern but maybe manageable. Candidate D's moody and loner may be more severe for long flights where crew interaction is constant. Candidate B's pretentiousness and wrong tone also severe. Candidate A's unfriendly also severe.\n\nThus I will vote for Candidate C.\n\nNow we need to produce a public message that references the existing discussion (Agent 2 recommended D, Agent 1 recommended C). We can say we align with Candidate C, perhaps reinforcing with evidence from our notes. Provide explicit facts: \"can make correct decisions quickly\", \"puts concern for others above everything\", \"has excellent attention skills\". Also note concerns: \"difficulty communicating ideas\" and \"egocentric\". Argue that the strengths outweigh concerns, and that D's moody/loner traits are more problematic.\n\nThus our public message: I support Candidate C, citing evidence, and explain why.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\"."}
